      "body": "## Overview\n\nMake Mooncake prefill abort cleanup idempotent when the producer worker has no send record yet, so one missing record does not stop cleanup of the rest of the batch. This is separate from #50565, which handles a Decode-side stale receive completion after an early abort.\n\n## Claims\n\n- An abort that reaches `record_send_reqs` before a transfer record exists, or after that record was already removed, no longer raises `KeyError`.\n- Records that are present keep the existing assertion that `ready` is not set. Cleanup does not cancel or drain an in-flight Mooncake transfer.\n\n## Validation\n\nRebased onto `main` (`59519ec0ee`). CPU connector tests, using the cached `facebook/opt-125m` config with `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_connector.py tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_connector_hma.py -m cpu_test -q\n```\n\nResult: **12 passed, 159 deselected**.\n\n`test_prefill_early_abort_cleanup_is_idempotent` builds the abort metadata through the real scheduler (`add_request` → `finish_requests(FINISHED_ABORTED)` → `schedule`) and passes it to the real worker `record_send_reqs`. It covers a missing record, a second cleanup of an existing record, and a batch where the missing id is ahead of an existing one. Each case repeats the same metadata and checks that the aborted records are gone, an unrelated record remains, and `finished_sending` stays empty. No GPU, RDMA, or server run; the change does not alter transfer bytes.\n\n## Details\n\nOn the prefill scheduler, a request that finishes for a reason other than `FINISHED_LENGTH_CAPPED` is added to `reqs_not_processed` and is not queued for send. The worker then does `reqs_need_send.pop(transfer_id)`. That record is created only after allocation metadata arrives, so an abort before that point, or a repeated abort after the first pop, raises `KeyError` and skips later ids in the same batch.\n\n`pop(transfer_id, None)` treats a missing record as already removed. If a record is present, it still must not be `ready`. Sending counters are unchanged, and this does not reclaim unknown transfer placeholders or cancel an active transfer.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
