      "body": "<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nNo active review issues remain for the producer-side early-abort cleanup change.\n\n**No open issues** 🎉\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nThis PR makes Mooncake’s producer-side early prefill abort cleanup idempotent, preventing a missing transfer record from interrupting cleanup of the remaining batch. It is separate from the Decode-side stale completion fix in #50565.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Ignore missing send records while preserving the not-ready assertion for existing records.\n- Add scheduler-to-worker regression coverage for missing, existing, and mixed records with repeated cleanup.\n- Document the cleanup behavior and clarify that it does not cancel or drain active transfers.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `vllm/​distributed/​kv_transfer/​kv_connector/​v1/​mooncake/​mooncake_connector.py` | Safely handles absent transfer records during abort cleanup. |\r\n| `tests/​v1/​kv_connector/​unit/​test_mooncake_connector.py` | Tests repeated and mixed-batch cleanup while preserving unrelated records. |\r\n| `docs/​features/​mooncake_connector_usage.md` | Documents early-abort cleanup guarantees and limits. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>",
